IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc9-support`

-- ccc9-sexual-evidence.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), ss 276 to 277: evidence of a complainant's sexual activity (the "rape shield"), the procedure for the
-- accused, for the prosecutor and by joint application, the publication bans, and reputation evidence. (Sections 276.2 to 276.5 are shown repealed.)
-- LAYER 1: the law as the text states it, from no one's point of view. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: see ccc9-assault-officer.l4 (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled). MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own
-- words (a flat negative, an "unless" or "if" gate that is closed, a bare "must" not met: NOTES.md, Marginal readings); NOTHING where the text limits its own scope,
-- lists without closing the list, is silent, or points outside the text.
-- Provisions that address only the judge, the prosecutor or the clerk are encoded for what they decide and for what they mean to the accused; the accused's own duties
-- (the application, the 60 days, the copy to the complainant, the publication bans) are rules with their time limits.
-- SEAMS taken as inputs: `by s 787(1)` (the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction: ccc29); the judge's satisfaction and the facts of an
-- application are plain facts the person states.

-- The acts of the regulative rules of this module (every constructor begins with its section label).
DECLARE `s 276.01 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 276.06(4) give a copy of the application to the accused and file it with the clerk of the court`
    `s 276.1(3) file a copy of the application with the clerk of the court`
    `s 276.1(4) consider the application in the absence of the applicants, without a hearing, and make a determination with reasons`
    `s 276.01(3) consider the application with the jury and the public excluded`
    `s 276.01(5) cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused`
    `s 276.02(1) exclude the jury and the public from the hearing`
    `s 276.02(3) inform the complainant of their right to be represented by counsel as soon as feasible`
    `s 276.02(4) determine whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2) and provide reasons`
    `s 276.03(1) publish, broadcast or transmit in any way a matter listed in subsection (1)`
    `s 276.04 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence`
    `s 276.07(1) publish, broadcast or transmit in any way a matter listed in subsection (1)`
    `s 276.08 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence`
    `s 276.06(5) exclude the jury and the public from the hearing`
    `s 276.06(7) determine whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2) and provide reasons`
    `s 276.1(6) direct the applicants as to the uses that they may and may not make of the evidence`
    `s 276.11(1) publish, broadcast or transmit in any way a matter listed in subsection (1)`
    `s 276.12 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence`


§ `Part VIII -- Evidence of the complainant's sexual activity (s 276)`

-- 276(1) and (2) apply in proceedings for the offences named by section number (R1; section 160 only for subsections (2) and (3)) "or any other offence ... that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose".
-- The named sections are tested by number; the open tail is a fact the person states.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(1)
-- src:5148 | Evidence of complainant’s sexual activity
-- src:5149 | 276 (1) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or any other offence under this Act, or any other Act of Parliament, that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose, evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, whether with the accused or with any other person, is not admissible to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant
@ref Criminal Code s 276(1) (src:5148-5149)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 276(1) the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the subsection applies` MEANS
        offence's `section` EQUALS 151 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 152 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153.1 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 155
     OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 160 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 170 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 171 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 172 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 173
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 271 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 272 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 273
     OR `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`

-- src:5148 | Evidence of complainant’s sexual activity
-- src:5149 | 276 (1) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or any other offence under this Act, or any other Act of Parliament, that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose, evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, whether with the accused or with any other person, is not admissible to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant
-- src:5150 | (a) is more likely to have consented to the sexual activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge; or
-- src:5151 | (b) is less worthy of belief.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(1) (src:5148-5151)
DECLARE `s 276(1) facts` HAS
    `the offence charged`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, by s 276(4) and (5)`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is more likely to have consented to the sexual activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is less worthy of belief`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- JUST TRUE: the evidence is not admissible for the inference. NOTHING: outside the named proceedings, or not evidence of sexual activity, or not offered for the inference: the subsection is limited by its own words and says nothing there.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(1); s 276(1)(a); s 276(1)(b)
-- src:5148 | Evidence of complainant’s sexual activity
-- src:5149 | 276 (1) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or any other offence under this Act, or any other Act of Parliament, that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose, evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, whether with the accused or with any other person, is not admissible to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant
-- src:5150 | (a) is more likely to have consented to the sexual activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge; or
-- src:5151 | (b) is less worthy of belief.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(1) (src:5148-5151)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 276(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(1) the evidence is not admissible to support the inference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 276(1) the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the subsection applies` (facts's `the offence charged`) (facts's `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or any other offence"
        IF facts's `the evidence is evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, by s 276(4) and (5)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sexual activity includes any communication"; whether the evidence is of sexual activity is itself not covered
        IF facts's `the evidence is evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, by s 276(4) and (5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity"
        IF facts's `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is more likely to have consented to the sexual activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge` OR facts's `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is less worthy of belief` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not admissible to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity"

DECLARE `s 276(2) who seeks to adduce the evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 276(2)(a) the accused or someone on the accused's behalf`
    `s 276(2)(b) the prosecutor or someone on the prosecutor's behalf`
    `s 276(2) someone else`

-- src:5152 | Conditions for admissibility
-- src:5153 | (2) In proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1), evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge, whether with the accused or with any other person, shall not be adduced unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice determines, in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be, that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1), is relevant to an issue at trial, is of specific instances of sexual activity and
-- src:5154 | (a) if sought to be adduced by or on behalf of the accused, has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice; or
-- src:5155 | (b) if sought to be adduced by or on behalf of the prosecutor, has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(2) (src:5152-5155)
DECLARE `s 276(2) facts` HAS
    `the offence charged`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `who seeks to adduce the evidence`   IS A `s 276(2) who seeks to adduce the evidence`
    `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has made a determination in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- "shall not be adduced unless the judge ... determines ...": JUST TRUE = the bar applies (a condition of the "unless" is unmet); JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met and the bar is lifted; NOTHING = outside the subsection.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(2); s 276(2)(a); s 276(2)(b)
-- src:5152 | Conditions for admissibility
-- src:5153 | (2) In proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1), evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge, whether with the accused or with any other person, shall not be adduced unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice determines, in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be, that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1), is relevant to an issue at trial, is of specific instances of sexual activity and
-- src:5154 | (a) if sought to be adduced by or on behalf of the accused, has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice; or
-- src:5155 | (b) if sought to be adduced by or on behalf of the prosecutor, has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(2) (src:5152-5155)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 276(2) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(2) the evidence is barred from being adduced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 276(1) the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the subsection applies` (facts's `the offence charged`) (facts's `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF NOT facts's `the evidence is of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge"
        IF facts's `who seeks to adduce the evidence` EQUALS `s 276(2) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) and (b) name only the accused and the prosecutor
        IF `the determination is complete` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be adduced unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice determines"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the determination is complete` MEANS
                facts's `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has made a determination in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be`
            AND facts's `the determination is that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1)`
            AND facts's `the determination is that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial`
            AND facts's `the determination is that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity`
            AND (   (facts's `who seeks to adduce the evidence` EQUALS `s 276(2)(a) the accused or someone on the accused's behalf` AND facts's `the determination is that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`)
                 OR (facts's `who seeks to adduce the evidence` EQUALS `s 276(2)(b) the prosecutor or someone on the prosecutor's behalf` AND facts's `the determination is that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`))

-- src:5156 | Factors that judge must consider
-- src:5157 | (3) In determining whether evidence is admissible under subsection (2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall take into account
@ref Criminal Code s 276(3) (src:5156-5157)
DECLARE `s 276(3) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 276(3)(a) the interests of justice, including the right of the accused to make a full answer and defence`
    `s 276(3)(b) society's interest in encouraging the reporting of sexual assault offences`
    `s 276(3)(c) whether there is a reasonable prospect that the evidence will assist in arriving at a just determination in the case`
    `s 276(3)(d) the need to remove from the fact-finding process any discriminatory belief or bias`
    `s 276(3)(e) the risk that the evidence may unduly arouse sentiments of prejudice, sympathy or hostility in the jury`
    `s 276(3)(f) the potential prejudice to the complainant's personal dignity and right of privacy`
    `s 276(3)(g) the right of the complainant and of every individual to personal security and to the full protection and benefit of the law`
    `s 276(3)(h) any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(3); s 276(3)(a); s 276(3)(b); s 276(3)(c); s 276(3)(d); s 276(3)(e); s 276(3)(f); s 276(3)(g); s 276(3)(h)
-- src:5156 | Factors that judge must consider
-- src:5157 | (3) In determining whether evidence is admissible under subsection (2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall take into account
-- src:5158 | (a) the interests of justice, including the right of the accused to make a full answer and defence;
-- src:5159 | (b) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of sexual assault offences;
-- src:5160 | (c) whether there is a reasonable prospect that the evidence will assist in arriving at a just determination in the case;
-- src:5161 | (d) the need to remove from the fact-finding process any discriminatory belief or bias;
-- src:5162 | (e) the risk that the evidence may unduly arouse sentiments of prejudice, sympathy or hostility in the jury;
-- src:5163 | (f) the potential prejudice to the complainant’s personal dignity and right of privacy;
-- src:5164 | (g) the right of the complainant and of every individual to personal security and to the full protection and benefit of the law; and
-- src:5165 | (h) any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(3) (src:5156-5165)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 276(3) factor`
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(3) the judge shall take the factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 276(3)(h) any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
        IF `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the factor relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(4)
-- src:5166 | Interpretation
-- src:5167 | (4) For the purpose of this section, sexual activity includes any communication made for a sexual purpose or whose content is of a sexual nature.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(4) (src:5166-5167)
GIVEN `it is a communication made for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its content is of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(4) the communication is sexual activity` MEANS
    IF `it is a communication made for a sexual purpose` OR `its content is of a sexual nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sexual activity includes any communication made for a sexual purpose or whose content is of a sexual nature"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276(5)
-- src:5168 | For greater certainty
-- src:5169 | (5) For the purposes of this section, and for greater certainty, evidence of sexual activity includes evidence of sexual inactivity.
@ref Criminal Code s 276(5) (src:5168-5169)
GIVEN `the evidence is evidence of sexual inactivity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(5) evidence of sexual inactivity is evidence of sexual activity` MEANS
    IF `the evidence is evidence of sexual inactivity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "evidence of sexual activity includes evidence of sexual inactivity"

§ `Part VIII -- Procedure for the accused (ss 276.01 to 276.05)`

-- "at least 60 days": the days from the earlier date to the later date (daydate `Day`), so 60 days is a difference of 60 or more; or "within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice".
-- The Interpretation Act's rules for "clear days" are not among the sources (fork F-days in NOTES.md). Used by s 276.01(4), s 276.06(4), s 276.1(3), s 278.12(5), s 278.21(5), s 278.3(5).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(4)
-- src:5178 | Hearing
-- src:5179 | (4) If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the application was made in accordance with subsection (2), that a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days previously or within any shorter interval that the judge, provincial court judge or justice may allow in the interests of justice, and that the evidence sought to be adduced is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the application and hold a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether the evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(4) (src:5178-5179)
GIVEN `the day the copy was given to the other side and filed with the clerk` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 276.01(4) the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` MEANS
        `s 270 helper: the days from the earlier date to the later date` `the day the copy was given to the other side and filed with the clerk` `the day of the hearing` AT LEAST 60
     OR `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`

-- A passive "may be made": an eligibility test, not a permission held by the accused (phrasebook entry 5.1). A "may" function with an "if"-like description: NOTHING outside it (ruling of 2026-11-12, fork in NOTES.md).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(1)
-- src:5172 | Application for hearing
-- src:5173 | 276.01 (1) Application may be made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice by or on behalf of the accused for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(1) (src:5172-5173)
GIVEN `the application is made by or on behalf of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.01(1) the application may be made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice for a hearing` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by or on behalf of the accused` AND `the application is made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice` AND `the application is for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Application may be made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice by or on behalf of the accused for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)"


-- "The application must be made in writing and must be accompanied by an affidavit setting out detailed particulars ... and a copy ... must be given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court."
-- A bare "must" not met is the text's no for this question (fork F in NOTES.md: the other reading is NOTHING).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(2)
-- src:5174 | Form and content
-- src:5175 | (2) The application must be made in writing and be accompanied by an affidavit setting out detailed particulars of the evidence that the accused seeks to adduce and the relevance of that evidence to an issue at trial, and a copy of the application and the affidavit must be given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(2) (src:5174-5175)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit sets out detailed particulars of the evidence that the accused seeks to adduce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit sets out the relevance of that evidence to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the application and the affidavit is given to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the application and the affidavit is filed with the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.01(2) the application meets the requirements of form and content` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing` AND `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit sets out detailed particulars of the evidence that the accused seeks to adduce` AND `the affidavit sets out the relevance of that evidence to an issue at trial` AND `a copy of the application and the affidavit is given to the prosecutor` AND `a copy of the application and the affidavit is filed with the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be made in writing and be accompanied by an affidavit"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(3)
-- src:5176 | Jury and public excluded
-- src:5177 | (3) The judge, provincial court judge or justice shall consider the application with the jury and the public excluded.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(3) (src:5176-5177)
GIVEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 276.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.01(3) the jury and the public shall be excluded when the application is considered` MEANS
    IF `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 276.01(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The judge, provincial court judge or justice shall consider the application with the jury and the public excluded"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(3)
-- src:5176 | Jury and public excluded
-- src:5177 | (3) The judge, provincial court judge or justice shall consider the application with the jury and the public excluded.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(3) (src:5176-5177)
GIVEN presiding IS A Party
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 276.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 276.01 act`
`s 276.01(3) the presiding officer's duty to exclude the jury and the public` MEANS
    IF `s 276.01(3) the jury and the public shall be excluded when the application is considered` `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 276.01(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY presiding
         MUST `s 276.01(3) consider the application with the jury and the public excluded`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY presiding BECAUSE "s 276.01(3): the application was considered with the jury or the public present"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: this is not a finding about any other case (the decision function answers NOTHING there)


-- (4): the judge shall grant the application and hold the hearing if satisfied of the three things; the second is the 60 days above.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(4)
-- src:5178 | Hearing
-- src:5179 | (4) If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the application was made in accordance with subsection (2), that a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days previously or within any shorter interval that the judge, provincial court judge or justice may allow in the interests of justice, and that the evidence sought to be adduced is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the application and hold a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether the evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(4) (src:5178-5179)
GIVEN `the application meets the requirements of form and content, by s 276.01(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence sought to be adduced is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.01(4) the judge shall grant the application and hold a hearing under section 276.02` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST `the application meets the requirements of form and content, by s 276.01(2)`, JUST (`the copy was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows`), JUST (`the evidence sought to be adduced is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2)`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the application was made in accordance with subsection (2), that a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days previously"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection (2) is itself not covered

-- The text states no time limit for the copy, so the rule carries no WITHIN.
