    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge, provincial court judge or justice grants the application and agrees to hold the hearing, the accused shall cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.01(5)
-- src:5180 | Copy to complainant
-- src:5181 | (5) If the judge, provincial court judge or justice grants the application and agrees to hold the hearing, the accused shall cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.01(5) (src:5180-5181)
GIVEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice grants the application and agrees to hold the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 276.01 act`
`s 276.01(5) the accused's duty to cause a copy to be given to the complainant` MEANS
    IF `s 276.01(5) the accused shall cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused` `the judge, provincial court judge or justice grants the application and agrees to hold the hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused`
         MUST `s 276.01(5) cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused`
