-- (4): "At the conclusion of the hearing, the judge ... shall determine whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible ... and shall provide reasons for that determination, and (a) ... (b) ... (c)".
-- The content requirements of (a), (b), (c) are tested here; the duty to determine and give reasons is the rule below. A bare "must" unmet is the text's no (fork F).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.02(4); s 276.02(4)(a); s 276.02(4)(b); s 276.02(4)(c)
-- src:5188 | Determination and reasons
-- src:5189 | (4) At the conclusion of the hearing, the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall determine whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2) and shall provide reasons for that determination, and
@ref Criminal Code s 276.02(4) (src:5188-5189)
GIVEN `the judge has determined whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has provided reasons for that determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not all of the evidence is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the part of the evidence that is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 276(3) that affected the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or any part of the evidence is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the manner in which that evidence is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.02(4) the determination and reasons meet the requirements` MEANS
    IF     `the judge has determined whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2)`
       AND `the judge has provided reasons for that determination`
       AND ((NOT `not all of the evidence is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the part of the evidence that is to be admitted`)
       AND `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 276(3) that affected the determination`
       AND ((NOT `all or any part of the evidence is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the manner in which that evidence is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall determine whether the evidence, or any part of it, is admissible under subsection 276(2) and shall provide reasons for that determination"

