-- src:5195 | Publication prohibited
-- src:5196 | 276.03 (1) A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5197 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 276.01(1);
-- src:5198 | (b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application made under subsection 276.01(1) or at a hearing under section 276.02;
-- src:5199 | (c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 276.01(4), unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the decision may be published, broadcast or transmitted;
-- src:5200 | (d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 276.02(4), unless that determination is that evidence is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.03(1) (src:5195-5200)
DECLARE `s 276.03(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 276.03(1)(a) the contents of an application made under subsection 276.01(1)`
    `s 276.03(1)(b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application or at a hearing under section 276.02`
    `s 276.03(1)(c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 276.01(4)`
    `s 276.03(1)(d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 276.02(4)`
    `s 276.03(1) any other matter`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.03(1); s 276.03(1)(a); s 276.03(1)(b); s 276.03(1)(c); s 276.03(1)(d)
-- src:5195 | Publication prohibited
-- src:5196 | 276.03 (1) A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5197 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 276.01(1);
-- src:5198 | (b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application made under subsection 276.01(1) or at a hearing under section 276.02;
-- src:5199 | (c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 276.01(4), unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the decision may be published, broadcast or transmitted;
-- src:5200 | (d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 276.02(4), unless that determination is that evidence is admissible or the judge, provincial court judge or justice, after taking into account the complainant’s right of privacy and the interests of justice, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.03(1) (src:5195-5200)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 276.03(1) matter`
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 276.03(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.03(1) the publication, broadcast or transmission of the matter is prohibited` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 276.03(1) any other matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following"
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 276.03(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs"
            IF `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 276.03(1.1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of the exception is itself not covered
            IF `the matter has an unless-clause that is met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the matter has an unless-clause that is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER matter
            WHEN `s 276.03(1)(a) the contents of an application made under subsection 276.01(1)` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `s 276.03(1)(b) any evidence taken, the information given or the representations made at the consideration of an application or at a hearing under section 276.02` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `s 276.03(1)(c) the decision of a judge, provincial court judge or justice under subsection 276.01(4)` THEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted`
            WHEN `s 276.03(1)(d) the determination made and the reasons provided under subsection 276.02(4)` THEN (`the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` OR `the determination is that evidence is admissible`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE

