    IF `s 276.01(4) the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` `the day the copy was given to the accused and filed with the clerk` `the day of the hearing` `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the application must be given to the accused and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing"

-- The prosecutor's duty as a rule, with its period: WITHIN the days from the day the application is made until 60 days before the hearing (counted in days, the trace's clock being the day the application is made).
-- Where the judge allows a shorter interval the text gives its length to the judge, so the rule states none (no duty arises under it).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.06(4)
-- src:5220 | Copy of the application
-- src:5221 | (4) A copy of the application must be given to the accused and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing or within any shorter interval that the judge, provincial court judge or justice may allow in the interests of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.06(4) (src:5220-5221)
GIVEN `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 276.01 act`
`s 276.06(4) the prosecutor's duty to give a copy to the accused and file it` MEANS
    IF `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN FULFILLED   -- the interval is the judge's to allow and the text states no length: no period is stated here (not a finding that the duty is met)
    ELSE PARTY `the prosecutor`
         MUST `s 276.06(4) give a copy of the application to the accused and file it with the clerk of the court`
         WITHIN (`s 270 helper: the days from the earlier date to the later date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the hearing` MINUS 60)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 276.06(4): the copy was not given to the accused and filed with the clerk at least 60 days before the hearing"

