-- src:5284 | 276.12 If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4), the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.12 (src:5283-5284)
GIVEN `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.12 the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that it may and may not make of the evidence` MEANS
    IF `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4), the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.12
-- src:5283 | Instruction to jury — use of evidence
-- src:5284 | 276.12 If evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4), the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of that evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.12 (src:5283-5284)
GIVEN presiding IS A Party
      `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 276.01 act`
`s 276.12 the judge's duty to instruct the jury` MEANS
    IF `s 276.12 the judge shall instruct the jury as to the uses that it may and may not make of the evidence` `evidence is admitted at trial on the basis of a determination made under subsection 276.1(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY presiding
         MUST `s 276.12 instruct the jury as to the uses that the jury may and may not make of the evidence`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY presiding BECAUSE "s 276.12: the jury was not instructed as to the uses of the evidence"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: the decision function answers JUST FALSE there, the text's own "if" being unmet, which is not a finding about any other case

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 276.13
-- src:5285 | Appeal
-- src:5286 | 276.13 For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 276.1(4) or (5) is deemed to be a question of law.
@ref Criminal Code s 276.13 (src:5285-5286)
GIVEN `it is a determination made under subsection 276.1(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276.13 the determination is deemed to be a question of law for the purposes of sections 675 and 676` MEANS
    IF `it is a determination made under subsection 276.1(4) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 675 and 676, a determination made under subsection 276.1(4) or (5) is deemed to be a question of law"

§ `Part VIII -- Reputation evidence (s 277)`

-- The named sections are tested by number (R1); section 160 only for subsections (2) and (3).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 277
-- src:5293 | Reputation evidence
-- src:5294 | 277 In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273, evidence of sexual reputation, whether general or specific, is not admissible for the purpose of challenging or supporting the credibility of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 277 (src:5293-5294)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the evidence is evidence of sexual reputation, whether general or specific` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is adduced for the purpose of challenging or supporting the credibility of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277 the evidence of sexual reputation is not admissible` MEANS
    IF     (   offence's `section` EQUALS 151 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 152 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153.1 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 155
            OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 160 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
            OR offence's `section` EQUALS 170 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 171 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 172 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 173
            OR offence's `section` EQUALS 271 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 272 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 273)
       AND `the evidence is evidence of sexual reputation, whether general or specific`
       AND `it is adduced for the purpose of challenging or supporting the credibility of the complainant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3) or section 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 or 273, evidence of sexual reputation, whether general or specific, is not admissible for the purpose of challenging or supporting the credibility of the complainant"
